Z||000000||sqoach||10-14-2001||08:11 PM||||My clutch pedal on my V6 SE 4spd is kinda hard to push down on. I let my friend drive it and he said something about it. Of course he has a new pick-up, so his is <I>much</I> easier. I couldn't even tell I was pressing the clutch down. I thought something was wrong with his! Anyway, I checked the pedal on my 2.5L 5spd and it is easier to press. Is something wrong with my pedal?<BR>Also, my pedal is bent down even with the brake pedal. Is this hard to change out?<P>I did a search, but didn't get much from it. If anyone can give me some advice or point me to a helpful thread, I'd appreciate it. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||4
Z||000001||ssalyers||10-14-2001||08:22 PM||||The clutch pedal is EXTREMELY easy to change.  I'm 6'1" 210 pounds and I can get under the dash to change it pretty easy.  <P>--Shawn||||reg||4
